{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/474250-renown-that-doesn-t-come-from-the-lunes","id":474250,"title":"Renown that doesn't come from the Lunes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T07:08:51-07:00","id":474250,"title":"Renown that doesn't come from the Lunes","content":"There's another thread going about whether the Renown dot you get from being part of a Tribe &quot;belongs&quot; to the Tribe (i.e. whether you lose it when you leave the Tribe to switch or for other reasons), and it got me thinking of other issues regarding Renown that seem to be only partially covered by the 2E book.<br /> <br /> First off, how do the Pure do it? They're big moon-haters, so they must not wait around for Lunes to brand their souls. The only thing I noticed in the 2E book about it was that the Blood Talon Siskur-Dah blurb said that Pure Renown marks are a fiery red insteady of a glowy silver. I've never read the Pure book, so I assume it's in there somewhere... <br /> <br /> Do Bale Hounds get special wound-born Renown marks? Being as they're only brought up sporadically in the 2E book, I know next to nothing about them, and almost all of that has been garnered from reading these forums for the past few months.<br /> <br /> If there are ways of getting Renown marks aside from getting them from Lunes, could Renown be a Totem boon? There's that Pure Bred (Purity) Merit on the Ivory Claw Blood-Hunter that someone (I think maybe Chris) said was an errata Merit meant to increase effective Renown under certain circumstance; if not an actual Renown dot as a Totem boon, would an effective dot that opened up the option to take aligned Facets and gave a +1 to those rolls but didn't, in and of itself, grant a free Facet be a reasonable thing for a Totem to grant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":".  noticed a typo 04-09-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:31:56-07:00","id":474281,"title":"","content":"Presumably the Pure do it the same way they did in first edition, which involves the pack or Pure society at large, with the guidance of their totem. Renown brands are not silver symbols engraved by Lunes, but scars and brands made painfully by your brethren.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are sort of up in the air, because they were made available as a series of options. Some of the options suggested that being a Bale Hound was in addition to a werewolf being a Forsaken or Pure. So you would still have your Lune-granted brands or your scars. The Lunes are not exactly anti-Bale Hound and would still offer renown to particular deeds. Alternatively, as the Ninth Tribe or a form of dark pantheism, they had a rite that allowed them to capture and bind Lunes, which they then tortured into submission and kept constantly mortally wounded. In case the Lunes weren't predisposed to granting you renown for some reason, you could have one ready to do it yourself, but otherwise their renown was 'regular' renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:02:06-07:00","id":474763,"title":"","content":"Has anyone else considered the idea of Renown points or Gift Facets as Totem boons? When I brought up the idea with my group, my ST didn't complain, but they were mostly for totems we weren't likely to take, anyway. I'd be interested to get some feedback on that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:11:04-07:00","id":474794,"title":"","content":"Right. I edited this whole thing pretty much after thinking about it.<br /> <br /> I'd say no. Totem boons are granted temporarily by the totem, if the totem ceases to exist or is forsaken by the pack, they lose the boon. In this case, I think the only time it would be appropriate would be either if the spirit is one of an aspect of renown, such as a spirit of honor or wisdom, or a spirit of deceit. Either way, I wouldn't allow the 'boon' renown to grant gifts due to the players gaining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:02:32-07:00","id":475008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/474250-renown-that-doesn-t-come-from-the-lunes?p=474794#post474794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. I edited this whole thing pretty much after thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious what you originally thought.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/474250-renown-that-doesn-t-come-from-the-lunes?p=474794#post474794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, I wouldn't allow the 'boon' renown to grant gifts due to the players gaining it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'boon' renown granting a bonus Facet seemed over the top to me, too. I had come up with a bunch of examples of Totem spirits for my group to consider; only two of them granted what I was calling &quot;a dot of effective [Renown]&quot;. One of them was taking a Crescent Moon Lune as our Totem (complete with a Persistent Madness Condition) and being granted an effective dot of Wisdom. The other was a Great Beast spirit that granted an effective dot of Purity and the Pack Kin Facet with it's 5XP worth of boon (3 for the dot, 2 for the Facet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:33:40-07:00","id":475051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/474250-renown-that-doesn-t-come-from-the-lunes?p=475008#post475008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what you originally thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I changed it because it was erroneous, mechanics-wise. From my point of view, at least. I mentioned that I'd only allow it if it was a Lune spirit totem that was bound to the pack after a great deed, which would justify the renown for it, since it was a renown-worthy deed and a Lune that could grant such things. I talked a bit about Lune totems, rare and dangerous, but then I realized that if you got renown for earning the totem, it would have been earned renown, not a boon granted by the totem that would disappear with said totem. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}